Alvaro,

There are some problems in your .csv and it's hard to know what to do with them:
Extra first line for years, I suppose.
Empty cells.
"ND" where it should be "NA".
An isolated column at the end.

Once you have these fixed, since you want to add year effects and the year-varying effect of agua, *one* way to do this is

yearlySiteCovs = data.frame(year = year, agua = as.numeric(unlist(t(a[,33:38]))))

Your secondary covariate (which is an observation/detection covariate, I assume) should be

obsCovs <-data.frame(secondary = as.factor(rep(c(1,2,3,4,5),S*T)))

Then, make your data object

umf = unmarkedMultFrame(y = y, siteCovs = site.cov, yearlySiteCovs = yearlySiteCovs, obsCovs = obsCovs, numPrimary = 6)

