Thanks for the comments and for the reference John. My rationale for using estimated psi is that it just seems intuitively nonsensical to use observed presence of cattle/people/hunting etc when I am implicitly acknowledging that these data may be a poor representation of the real occurrence of these threats.  And I do appreciate that more explicit co-occurrence models can be fit elsewhere but in the immediate term I need to find a way of presenting the analysis of these, and other, data within one relatively user-friendly environment, and for various reasons that is going to be unmarked.

